From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: initialise channel state before registering
 misc devices

Opening a misc device can happen while RPMsg probe is still running.
Initialise the refcount, lock, lists and invocation state before
registering these devices so the open path can use the channel state.
This also publishes the domain and RPMsg device before registration.

Jianping Li identified the problem and originally moved kref_init() in
the first version of the Qualcomm SSR series. The Piano adaptation
also moved the remaining channel state used by opens and invocations.
This patch reproduces that ordering from the existing Piano kernel.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261007084447.922-2-jianping.li@oss.qualcomm.com
Link: https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/kernel/commit/a0741420ba061510b843fa98e40a1c3fa513e131
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
---
 drivers/misc/fastrpc.c | 23 +++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
index 1cf56227373f02200c4f22a4c8fe25e8c10fde81..bb6403383d80f3078961b0f4686d3a5c801c0e5b 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -2646,6 +2646,17 @@ static int fastrpc_rpmsg_probe(struct rpmsg_device *rpdev)
 	data->poll_mode_supported = soc_data->poll_mode_supported ||
 		of_machine_get_match(fastrpc_poll_supported_machines);
 
+	kref_init(&data->refcount);
+	atomic_set(&data->ctx_seq, 0);
+	atomic_set(&data->teardown, 0);
+	init_waitqueue_head(&data->ssr_wait_queue);
+	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&data->users);
+	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&data->invoke_interrupted_mmaps);
+	spin_lock_init(&data->lock);
+	idr_init(&data->ctx_idr);
+	data->domain_id = domain_id;
+	data->rpdev = rpdev;
+
 	switch (domain_id) {
 	case ADSP_DOMAIN_ID:
 	case MDSP_DOMAIN_ID:
@@ -2673,20 +2684,8 @@ static int fastrpc_rpmsg_probe(struct rpmsg_device *rpdev)
 		goto err_free_data;
 	}
 
-	kref_init(&data->refcount);
-	atomic_set(&data->ctx_seq, 0);
-
 	rdev->dma_mask = &data->dma_mask;
 	dma_set_mask_and_coherent(rdev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
-	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&data->users);
-	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&data->invoke_interrupted_mmaps);
-	spin_lock_init(&data->lock);
-	idr_init(&data->ctx_idr);
-	atomic_set(&data->teardown, 0);
-	data->invoke_cnt = 0;
-	init_waitqueue_head(&data->ssr_wait_queue);
-	data->domain_id = domain_id;
-	data->rpdev = rpdev;
 	dev_set_drvdata(&rpdev->dev, data);
 
 	err = of_platform_populate(rdev->of_node, NULL, NULL, rdev);
